WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.875
Here's some good news.

00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:01.835
The president of China

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:02.585
and the United States

00:00:02.585 --> 00:00:03.878
just met in San Francisco,

00:00:03.878 --> 00:00:05.338
and one of the things they discussed

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:06.548
was pandas.

00:00:06.548 --> 00:00:07.549
A few decades ago, China

00:00:07.549 --> 00:00:09.426
gave a bunch of pandas to the U.S.

00:00:09.426 --> 00:00:10.010
National Zoo

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.136
here in Washington, D.C.,

00:00:11.136 --> 00:00:13.763
as a sign of friendship and diplomacy.

00:00:13.763 --> 00:00:15.515
But recently they took the pandas back

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:16.558
because of the increasing

00:00:16.558 --> 00:00:18.059
tensions between these two countries.

00:00:18.059 --> 00:00:18.893
But after this meeting

00:00:18.893 --> 00:00:20.061
between these two presidents,

00:00:20.061 --> 00:00:21.062
Xi Jinping suggested

00:00:21.062 --> 00:00:22.814
that they should send the pandas back

00:00:22.814 --> 00:00:24.232
as a gesture of their friendship.

00:00:24.232 --> 00:00:25.817
I mean, it's kind of bizarre

00:00:25.817 --> 00:00:27.193
that diplomatic relations

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:28.194
between the two most powerful

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.030
countries is being measured in pandas,

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:30.947
but hey, I'll take it.

00:00:30.947 --> 00:00:31.823
If you want to better understand

00:00:31.823 --> 00:00:33.575
global politics, follow along for more.

